[2026-09-24T00:56:48.644+08:00] [TestGenerator][REQ-1]   "summary": "Coverage by layer for REQ-1 (passenger registration). Backend unit: registerValidation.test.js covers every field rule (username regex/boundaries, password 12–128 with all char classes, confirm equality, ID/passenger type option membership, name 2–100 trimmed, idNumber 6–30 ASCII, email ≤254, +84 9-digit / +86 11-digit phone rules, agreement). Backend integration: accountsRepository.test.js (isolated harness) verifies case-insensitive username/email lookup, unique-violation rejection, session create/auth/delete and no hash leakage; authService.test.js covers registerAccount field-code merging (DUPLICATE_USERNAME/EMAIL), session token lifecycle (64-hex token) and cookie contract; authRoutes.test.js (supertest, harness-before-import ordering) drives POST /api/auth/register (200 envelope + tb_session httpOnly cookie + /api/auth/me round trip), per-field 400 VALIDATION_FAILED codes, and logout clearing sessions. Frontend unit: registerValidation.test.ts asserts the exact dropdown option sets (+86/+84), passwordStrength 0–3 monotonicity and Chinese error messages mirroring backend; registerApi.test.ts mocks the shared apiClient for ok/field-error/401/logout paths. Frontend integration: RegisterPage.test.tsx locks the stable Chinese accessible-name contract (labels natively associated, initial select values 请选择证件类型/请选择乘客类型/+86, 3-segment strength meter via data-testid), blocks submission on missing/mismatched/unsigned-agreement input with role=alert Chinese errors and no API call, and asserts success navigates to / with the session refreshed; homePage.test.tsx (shared scope) verifies the guest Register link to /register and signed-in username + `Sign out` link. E2E (backend/test-e2e/register.e2e.spec.js) compiles all three scenarios with unique-per-run demo identities (tb-user-<ts>-<rand>, +84/912345678), verifying: valid registration → navigation to /, username + Sign out visible, /api/auth/me 200, session persists across reload; invalid submissions (unsigned agreement, password mismatch, bad username) show visible Chinese errors and never produce a session (me 401) with full per-submit input resets; duplicate username and case-insensitive duplicate email are rejected in fresh contexts leaving the original account intact. Owned behavior is RED on the design skeleton (empty repos/routes/pages), satisfying the green-baseline gate.",
